[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Read report by report, it holds two
problems. Each got a ticket of its own, and both are now closed.

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {filed} />

<Callout>
#4471 closed on 5 October. <code>parser</code>: fixed (fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales).
<code>hint</code>: won't fix, the booking-v3 form is retired.
</Callout>

## The two problems

**`parser`: day and month swap.** The shared parser reads every date month first, and every
tenant on file writes the day first. "4 March turned into 3 April." Fixed: the parser now reads dd/mm
for EU locales.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form asks for the wrong order.** Its date field prints `MM/DD/YYYY`
but reads the date day first. People type what the hint says, and the booking swaps. Only form
reports from tenants on booking-v3. The parser fix does not touch it. Won't fix: booking-v3 is retired, so the
hint goes with it.

**Read as a one-day move.** The desk read a few `parser` reports as a date landing a day early
(`desk-notes.json`), for example "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."
The cause follows the tenant, so they stay under `parser` and are footnoted under the table. If
these keep coming now the parser fix is out, open a ticket for them.

## How they were told apart

- Counted by report id: the export repeats some rows across its pages.
- Cause from the tenant (where they are, which form they run) and the report itself, not from
  the intake tag. Intake guesses from the reporter's browser and is wrong for many of these.
- Every report body was read: they describe a day and month swap, apart from the few the
  desk read as a one-day move (footnoted above).

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone, and the
[triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) says "when unsure, merge". Both bugs share the same subjects
("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"), so both landed in one ticket. Merging on
cause, as the triage explorer already checks, would have kept them apart. That needs a new
decision record to replace 0001.

